Compile hfxbase/hfx_compression_core_methods.F without loop vectorization when using GCC 15.
With GCC 15.2.0 and -march=x86-64-v3 or higher (any AVX2 or AVX-512 target), the loop vectorizer
turns the ints2bits_* routines into code that stores wrong packed words for several bit widths
(10, 12, 15, 26-28, 37-39, 41, 44), while bits2ints_* stay correct. The HFX in-core integral
storage and the tensor compression in qs_tensors.F then return wrong values, which shows up as
wrong energies in the HFX, TDDFPT-force, MP2-gradient and GW regression tests and as failed
Cholesky decompositions in the low-scaling RPA/GW tests (see https://github.com/cp2k/cp2k/issues/4774).
-fno-tree-loop-vectorize for this file alone restores bit-identical packing.
Author: Rohit Goswami
--- cp2k-2026.2.orig/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ cp2k-2026.2/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1696,3 +1696,14 @@
+# GCC 15 loop-vectorizes the ints2bits_* packing routines into code that stores
+# wrong bits when AVX2 or AVX-512 is enabled, which corrupts in-core HFX
+# integrals and compressed tensors.
+if(CMAKE_Fortran_COMPILER_ID STREQUAL "GNU"
+   AND CMAKE_Fortran_COMPILER_VERSION VERSION_GREATER_EQUAL 15
+   AND CMAKE_Fortran_COMPILER_VERSION VERSION_LESS 16)
+  set_source_files_properties(
+    ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/hfxbase/hfx_compression_core_methods.F
+    PROPERTIES COMPILE_OPTIONS "-fno-tree-loop-vectorize")
+endif()
+
 # set the __SHORT_FILE__ per file for CP2K sources
 foreach(cp2k_src ${CP2K_SRCS} ${CP2K_PROGS_F_FYPP})
   # add_fypp_sources returns a path in the current binary dir
